The legal texts are Norwegian laws and decisions of public authorities, as officially announced in
Norsk Lovtidend avd. I and published by Lovdata:

  Inneholder data under norsk lisens for offentlige data (NLOD) tilgjengeliggjort av Lovdata.
  Contains data under the Norwegian licence for Open Government data (NLOD) distributed by Lovdata.
  NLOD 2.0: https://data.norge.no/nlod/no/2.0
  Source: https://api.lovdata.no/publicData, retrieved 29 October 2026.

Laws, regulations, court decisions and other decisions of public authorities are not protected by
copyright in Norway (åndsverkloven, lov 15. juni 2018 nr. 40, § 14).

Changes made by Lexifina: each announcement's amendment instructions were applied by code to the text
before it; each version was converted to one Markdown file per provision, one ledd or list item per line;
spacing, quotes, dashes in number ranges and list labels were normalised; Lovdata's amendment notes and
editorial "(Opphevet ...)" lines were left out of the text; and the versions were arranged as git commits
credited to the decisions and laws that made each change. The wording of the law was not changed.
Lovdata does not endorse this repository.

Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages, the tables and the
tools) are dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode
